Instead of manually creating:

HttpServlet

Spring gives us:

@Controller






Example:

@Controller
public class StudentController {

    @RequestMapping("/student")
    public String student() {

        return "student";
    }
}




What happens?

Browser:

/student

↓

Spring finds:

student()

↓

returns:

"student"

↓

Spring looks for the corresponding view.

With JSP, for example:

student.jsp
